"text": "Then there's the acceleration. In a run at the event, Tesla showed zero to sixty in 0.81 seconds. That's Tesla's own test. Nobody independent has timed it. For perspective, that averages about three and a half times the pull of gravity: far more than ordinary road tires can grip on their own. So Tesla leans on thrusters here too. It says they push harder than the tires could. And that's where the versions split. Performance is the road-ready two-seater, with the suction system. Thrust adds rear cold-gas thrusters. Rocket is invite-only, seats one, and has the full flight system\u2026 and Tesla's own page says Rocket is not approved for public road use.",
